ACTION (planned, pre-execution):
  Forking MeanRev_AsymLS_Pt2.ipynb from Pt1 (Pt1 left intact and re-
  runnable). Single change in Pt2 vs Pt1:

    Feature change: ret_5 is now RESIDUALIZED.
      Pt1: ret_5 = stock_5d_return
      Pt2: ret_5 = stock_5d_return - equal_weight_PIT_market_5d_return

  Rationale: on a day the market moves +3%, every stock has "positive
  ret_5" even though only some genuinely outperformed on an idiosyncratic
  basis. Raw ret_5 loses discriminating power on strong-market days.
  Residualizing makes the feature a pure cross-sectional dislocation
  signal (stock-specific over/underperformance vs peers), which is the
  quantity that actually mean-reverts.

  Literature: Lehmann 1990, Lo-MacKinlay 1988, Khandani-Lo 2007 — residual
  reversal consistently shows 30-50% higher Sharpe than raw reversal, and
  crucially survives bull markets better (which is the 2022-2026 regime
  we're testing on).

  Other features unchanged (rsi_2, dist_bb, vol_20, volume_z still raw).
  Target still raw fwd_5 (we earn raw returns, so we optimize for raw).

  Outputs redirected to results/mean_rev_pt2/ so Pt1 artifacts are
  preserved. Optuna re-run fresh because best params may shift when
  feature semantics change.

  Execution next; results will be logged in a follow-up entry.
